SoapyAirspy: report the device's errors, and the settings it accepted

The module ignored libairspy's result for every setting it writes, and
updated what it reports before the write:

- setFrequency() kept the new frequency and ignored airspy_set_freq(),
  so a refused tune left the device on the old channel while
  getFrequency() reported the new one.
- setSampleRate() only kept the request, and getSampleRate() returned it.
  activateStream() and a read with a rate change pending wrote it later
  and ignored both airspy_set_samplerate() and airspy_start_rx():
  activateStream() returned success for a stream that never started, or
  that ran at the old rate.
- setGain() and setGainMode() kept the new LNA, mixer, VGA or AGC
  setting and ignored the write.

Each write is now checked, and what the module reports changes only once
the device has taken it. A refused setting throws std::runtime_error,
which SoapySDR's C API turns into an error code. setSampleRate() writes
the rate at once, so getSampleRate() returns a rate the device accepted;
on a running stream it stops, writes and restarts, as a pending rate did,
and a refused rate leaves the stream running on the rate it had.
activateStream() and a read that applies a pending rate return
SOAPY_SDR_STREAM_ERROR when the rate write or the start fails, and the
rate stays pending. setGainMode() whose mixer AGC write fails puts the
LNA AGC back as it was.

dsd-neo applies this patch to the SoapyAirspy module it builds for its
Windows release.

Generated against SoapyAirspy 9a906cac218bf07a7acd31efa1f2954c3a44ea4b.

